  "question": {
    "text": "Two concentric coils of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> turns each are placed in the same plane. Their radii are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and carry&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp; and&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> current respectively in opposite directions. The magnetic induction (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tesla</mi></math>) at the center is",
